#
# Frames analyzer-quick must refuse, plus one valid live-form frame
# (candump without -l, which prints "[8]" instead of "#").
#
# analyzer-quick has no NMEA 2000 PGN table, so a 29-bit identifier is not a
# Quick message and must be refused rather than decoded through the J1939 bit
# layout. Run with -fixtime so the error log is reproducible.
#
  can0  6C2   [8]  C1 18 00 00 00 00 00 00
  vcan0  00000100##1000000000000000
(1502979136.606111) vcan0 18EEFF05#04A9FFFFADFF
  vcan0  6C1#R
#
# The hard case: an extended identifier whose value happens to land inside the
# Quick range. Its numeric value is 0x6C1, so a value test alone would decode
# it as Quick PGN 1729. Only the printed width says it is 29-bit, and the NMEA
# 2000 analyzer already refuses it -- the two builds must not disagree.
#
(1502979137.706111) vcan0 000006C1#C1186B0000000200
